{"name":"Wild Iris","hex":"#2f2f4a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wild","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Untamed; not domesticated.","Especially, being of the wild type: being of an unbroken ancestral line of undomesticated animals, as opposed to being feral, being an undomesticated animal whose ancestors were domesticated."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Inaccurately; not on target.","Intended to be synchronized with film or video but recorded separately."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wild"},{"term":"iris","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the genus Iris, common in the northern hemisphere, and generally having attractive blooms (See  Iris (plant) on  Wikipedia.Wikipedia ).","The contractile membrane perforated by the pupil, which adjusts to control the amount of light reaching the retina, and which forms the colored portion of the eye (See  Iris (anatomy) on  Wikipedia.Wikipedia )."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To open or close in the manner of an iris.","To cause (something) to shine with the colours of the rainbow; to make iridescent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iris"}],"entries":[{"title":"Iris (plant)","blocks":[{"text":"Iris is a flowering plant genus of 320 accepted species with showy flowers. As well as being the scientific name, iris is also widely used as a common name for all Iris species, as well as some belonging to other closely related genera. A common name for some species is flags, while the plants of the subgenus Scorpiris are widely known as junos, particularly in horticulture. It is a popular garden flower."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iris_(plant)"},{"title":"Dietes grandiflora","blocks":[{"text":"Dietes grandiflora, commonly named fortnight lily, large wild iris, African iris or fairy iris, is a rhizomatous perennial plant of the Iris Family (Iridaceae) with long, rigid, sword-like green leaves. This species is common in horticulture in its native South Africa, where it is often used in public gardens, beautification of commercial premises and along roadsides."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Dietes_grandiflora_La_Brea.jpg/330px-Dietes_grandiflora_La_Brea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dietes_grandiflora"},{"title":"Wild Iris (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Wild Iris is a 2001 American drama television film directed by Daniel Petrie, written by Kent Broadhurst, and starring Gena Rowlands and Laura Linney, with Emile Hirsch, Lee Tergesen, and Fred Ward in supporting roles. It aired on Showtime on August 5, 2001."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0f/Wild_Iris_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Iris_(film)"},{"title":"Iris (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Iris is an ambiguous color term, usually referring to shades ranging from blue-violet to violet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Unidentified_Iris_Chanticleer_Purple_2868px.jpg/330px-Unidentified_Iris_Chanticleer_Purple_2868px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iris_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Iris_rhizome_p1150371.jpg/500px-Iris_rhizome_p1150371.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Iris_rhizome_p1150371.jpg/1280px-Iris_rhizome_p1150371.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Iris_rhizome_p1150371.jpg/500px-Iris_rhizome_p1150371.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rhizomes of ornamental irises","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIris_rhizome_p1150371.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Parts_of_an_iris_flower.jpg/500px-Parts_of_an_iris_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Parts_of_an_iris_flower.jpg/500px-Parts_of_an_iris_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration of an iris flower with highlighted parts of the flower","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AParts_of_an_iris_flower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Iris_reichenbachii.JPG/500px-Iris_reichenbachii.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Iris_reichenbachii.JPG/1280px-Iris_reichenbachii.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Iris_reichenbachii.JPG/500px-Iris_reichenbachii.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Iris reichenbachii fruit","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIris_reichenbachii.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Iris_persica_%28Sowerby%29.jpg/500px-Iris_persica_%28Sowerby%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Iris_persica_%28Sowerby%29.jpg/500px-Iris_persica_%28Sowerby%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A member of subgenus S